ok   the adapter is mysql and connects to the configured URL
ok   quote_ident wraps a name in backticks and doubles an embedded one
ok   upsert_tail is the row alias's ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE c = excluded.c, c = c without columns
ok   LAST_INSERT_ID marks: 0 for an INSERT that made no id, else its first
ok   table_names lists the tables of the connected database
ok   health_query answers one row
ok   foreign_keys_off and foreign_keys_on toggle the session's checks
ok   reset_sequences sets AUTO_INCREMENT back so ids start again at 1
ok   foreign_key_violation describes the first dangling row, and the migrator's check lists them
ok   foreign_key_violation and the migrator's check name an id-less table's row by its foreign key column
ok   transactional_ddl? is false; ddl_statements is MySQL's DDL; schema_migrations has a VARCHAR key
ok   now_epoch_usec_sql reads the clock in UTC epoch microseconds
ok   the relation pieces: a float total, a derived table's alias, LIKE's escape, no limit, a window of ids
ok   the schema readers answer name/type/notnull/dflt_value/pk, indexes and foreign keys
ok   Test::Database's clear empties a table; the mark is the table cybertrain_test_marker on MySQL
ok   the timetable and feed statements: a row never moves backwards, a missing one is added once
ok   the cache and lease writes answer whether a row changed
